From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] config: read the system client options from all three UAPI tiers
Source: no upstream commit; written for Nex against Looking Glass B7
Upstream: not submitted. The client hard-codes one system-wide options file, so
 a distribution cannot ship a default that a boot or an administrator may
 override. The change below adds the generic /usr/lib, /run, and /etc order and
 names no Nex path, so any Linux system that follows the UAPI configuration
 files specification can use it.

config_load() read exactly one system-wide file, /etc/looking-glass-client.ini,
before it read the user's own files. A package could not ship a default set of
client options below /usr, and a boot-time tool that knows the host's
shared-memory device or window geometry had nowhere to put a temporary file.

Read the package file below /usr/lib first, then the temporary file below /run,
then the administrator file below /etc, and overlay each onto the previous
ones. That matches what the client already does for its user files: option_load
replaces only the options a file names, so a higher tier overrides the options
it sets and leaves the rest alone. A missing file at any tier is skipped
exactly as the single /etc file already was, and the user files, the command
line, and app:configFile still come afterwards and still win.

diff -urN a/client/src/config.c b/client/src/config.c
--- a/client/src/config.c
+++ b/client/src/config.c
@@ -564,14 +564,29 @@
   option_register(options);
 }
 
+// The system-wide option files, lowest priority first: the immutable package
+// default, then temporary policy that one boot owns, then lasting
+// administrator policy. Each file is overlaid onto the previous ones, so a
+// later file overrides only the options it names.
+static const char * globalConfigFiles[] =
+{
+  "/usr/lib/looking-glass-client.ini",
+  "/run/looking-glass-client.ini",
+  "/etc/looking-glass-client.ini"
+};
+
 bool config_load(int argc, char * argv[])
 {
   // load any global options first
   struct stat st;
-  if (stat("/etc/looking-glass-client.ini", &st) >= 0 && S_ISREG(st.st_mode))
+  for(size_t i = 0; i < sizeof(globalConfigFiles) / sizeof(*globalConfigFiles); ++i)
   {
-    DEBUG_INFO("Loading config from: /etc/looking-glass-client.ini");
-    if (!option_load("/etc/looking-glass-client.ini"))
+    const char * file = globalConfigFiles[i];
+    if (stat(file, &st) < 0 || !S_ISREG(st.st_mode))
+      continue;
+
+    DEBUG_INFO("Loading config from: %s", file);
+    if (!option_load(file))
       return false;
   }
 
